# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
# A stutter on demand: G5 tapped (let go within the tap window), on any screen. Each tap the next kind: a simple one,
# a complex one, none; G5 blinks while one waits, slowly for a simple one (400 ms), quickly for a complex one
# (125 ms). It plays on the next group's last bar that isn't an intro's or an outro's, then G5 goes dark. The first
# song is 56 bars at 81 BPM (2963 ms a bar): an 8-bar intro, four 8-bar grooves (no lead), two lead blocks. Queued in
# the intro's second bar, it waits out the intro and lands on the first groove's last bar (bar 16, from 0: 15), a bar
# the song's own stutters skip (its first pass without the lead).
listen
wait 1400
tap PLAY
wait 3000
expect stutter 0
expect stutter_blink 0
# a tap: a simple one
tapkey 26
wait 50
said STUTTER SIMPLE
expect stutter 1
expect stutter_blink 400
expect hold -1
# again while it waits: a complex one
tapkey 26
wait 50
said STUTTER COMPLEX
expect stutter 2
expect stutter_blink 125
# a third: cancelled, G5 dark
tapkey 26
wait 50
said STUTTER OFF
expect stutter 0
expect stutter_blink 0
expect key_lit <67108864
# on another screen too (Sections): twice, a complex one
tap SEL
wait 50
said SECTIONS
tapkey 26
wait 50
tapkey 26
wait 50
said STUTTER COMPLEX
expect stutter 2
shot stutter-queued.png
# the intro passes; it waits, G5 blinking (bar 12, from 0: 11, about 34.6 s in)
wait 29496
expect section 1
expect stutter 2
expect stutter_blink 125
expect stutter_bar -1
# the first groove's last bar (bar 16, from 0: 15; 45.9-48.9 s): it lands there, a complex figure
wait 12800
expect bar 15
expect stutter_bar 15
expect stutter_fig >2
expect stutter 2
# its replays (the bar's 15th 16th, about 48.6 s): the mix stutters
wait 1050
expect stuttering 1
# the next bar: played, OFF again, nothing waiting
wait 2000
expect bar 16
expect stutter 0
expect stutter_bar -1
expect stutter_blink 0
shot stutter-played.png
# stopped, a tap queues one all the same (G5 blinks); PLAY: the song goes on from there, the stutter waiting in it
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect playing 0
tapkey 26
wait 50
said STUTTER SIMPLE
expect stutter 1
expect stutter_blink 400
tap PLAY
wait 1500
expect playing 1
expect stutter 1
# pressed as a finger does (Sam, 2026-11-14: a 16th at the song's tempo, 185 ms here, was shorter than a real tap):
# let go within the tap window (sthold.h's STH_TAP_MS), each press a tap, the next kind, said; the hold never caught
# (hold_in < 0: no catch since that press)
wait 400
key 26 down
wait 80
key 26 up
wait 50
said STUTTER COMPLEX
expect stutter 2
expect hold -1
expect hold_in <0
wait 400
key 26 down
wait 150
key 26 up
wait 50
said STUTTER OFF
expect stutter 0
expect hold_in <0
wait 400
key 26 down
wait 250
key 26 up
wait 50
said STUTTER SIMPLE
expect stutter 1
expect hold_in <0
# held 400 ms: the hold (STUTTER said once past the window), nothing queued: still the simple one
wait 400
key 26 down
wait 400
said STUTTER
key 26 up
wait 300
expect stutter 1
expect hold -1
# at the FM-1's pace: the keys read only between redraws, about 90 ms apart (uiframe), so a press measures up to a
# frame longer, or shorter (80 ms: from a frame's middle, seen down for one frame). The same taps; held 600 ms, the hold
uiframe 90
wait 45
key 26 down
wait 80
key 26 up
wait 200
said STUTTER COMPLEX
expect stutter 2
expect hold_in <0
wait 400
key 26 down
wait 150
key 26 up
wait 200
said STUTTER OFF
expect stutter 0
expect hold_in <0
wait 400
key 26 down
wait 250
key 26 up
wait 200
said STUTTER SIMPLE
expect stutter 1
expect hold_in <0
wait 400
key 26 down
wait 600
said STUTTER
expect hold 0
expect hold_ms >319
key 26 up
wait 300
expect stutter 1
expect hold -1
uiframe 0
